        "overview_ar": "The Arab Academy for Science, Technology and Maritime Transport (AASTMT) is a regional, non-profit educational organization affiliated with the League of Arab States, established in 1972 in Alexandria, Egypt. Unlike a typical single-campus Egyptian private university, AASTMT operates across at least seven campuses, with many of its colleges duplicated across multiple campuses. AASTMT's degrees are recognized by Egypt's Supreme Council of Universities, and several programs (particularly Engineering) hold accreditation from international bodies including ABET (USA) and UK professional institutes (IMechE, IMarEST, IET, ICE, IStructE, RIBA). AASTMT marked 50+ years of operation as of 2022 and serves over 30,000 students. It is historically best known for maritime transport education but has expanded significantly into engineering, computing, business, medicine, dentistry, pharmacy, artificial intelligence, law, archaeology, and the arts.",
