        "description": "Nahda University in Beni Suef (NUB) is a private university located in New Beni Suef City, Egypt, established in 2006 by Republican Decree. NUB describes itself as the first private university in Upper Egypt, founded through the efforts of its professors to develop education in the region. NUB comprises 10 faculties: Business Administration, Computer Science, Oral and Dental Medicine, Engineering, Mass Communication and Applied Languages, Medicine, Pharmacy, Physical Therapy, Fine Arts, and Nursing. NUB's Faculty of Medicine was developed in partnership with the Medical University of Vienna, and its Faculty of Oral and Dental Medicine follows the curriculum of the Vienna School of Dentistry. NUB's Faculty of Pharmacy was the first accredited private pharmacy college in Upper Egypt (NAQAAE accreditation, Decree No. 191, July 2019), and its Faculty of Business Administration and Faculty of Engineering hold institutional/program accreditations (NAQAAE 2023; ACAET for Engineering, May 2023).",
