        "overview": "Badr University in Assiut (BUA) is a leading educational beacon in the heart of Upper Egypt, combining diverse disciplines and scientific innovation to provide high-quality education and support sustainable development in the region. BUA is part of CIRA Education, the largest integrated provider of educational services in the Egyptian private sector. The university emphasizes embracing diversity, individuality, and encouraging a culture of open-mindedness. It offers a wide range of undergraduate programs across multiple schools, including Artificial Intelligence, Biotechnology, Physical Therapy, Linguistics, Pharmacy, Nursing, and Law. BUA also provides community services through its Community Services Center, Training, Languages, and Translation Center, and the Child University Program. The university fosters entrepreneurship and international partnerships, aiming to empower students to make meaningful changes in their communities.",
