        "overview": "Alexandria Higher Institute for Engineering & Technology (AIET) is a leading engineering institution under the supervision of the Ministry of Higher Education in Egypt. Established in 1997 in the Smouha district of Alexandria, near Sidi Gaber train station, it is the first private engineering institute in Alexandria. The institute offers a Bachelor's degree in Engineering across four scientific departments. AIET aims to provide distinguished education that combines theoretical concepts with practical applications, fostering a comprehensive learning experience for students. This includes engaging in scientific, cultural, artistic, and sports activities, as well as practical training in companies and factories to prepare students for the job market. The institute also emphasizes community service and interaction. The educational process is subject to continuous evaluation by the Quality Assurance Unit, which operates according to the standards of the National Authority for Quality Assurance and Accreditation in Education (NAQAAE), particularly in institutional capacity and educational effectiveness. Additionally, AIET supports research activities for faculty members, assistants, and students through a specialized research unit.",
